From: Armada OS source-only kernel review
Subject: [PATCH RFC] soc: qcom: modemsmem: preserve deferred probe from SMEM provider

When SMEM is not initialized, qcom_smem_alloc() may return
-EPROBE_DEFER and qcom_smem_get() may return ERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER).
The original modemsmem probe collapses both into -ENOMEM, preventing
the driver core from queuing the device for deferred probing.

Preserve -EPROBE_DEFER only, retaining the original -ENOMEM behavior
for all other allocation/get errors and size mismatch. Do not change
existing-item (-EEXIST) handling or SMEM content initialization.

Review-only candidate. Both original and patched modemsmem ARM64 objects
compiled against the pinned Redbull 4.19 source in GitHub CI (run
45324044445). This is compile-only evidence, not a boot or modem test.
Not deployed on the Pixel 5a, merged, or sent upstream.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/modemsmem/modemsmem.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/modemsmem/modemsmem.c
@@ -175,11 +175,19 @@ static int modem_smem_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 			sizeof(struct modem_smem_type));
 	if (ret && ret != -EEXIST) {
 		dev_err(dev, "smem alloc fail\n");
+		if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+			return ret;
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
 
 	modem_smem = qcom_smem_get(QCOM_SMEM_HOST_ANY, SMEM_ID_VENDOR0, &size);
-	if (IS_ERR(modem_smem) || size != sizeof(struct modem_smem_type)) {
+	if (IS_ERR(modem_smem)) {
 		dev_err(dev, "Get modem_smem pointer failed\n");
+		if (PTR_ERR(modem_smem) == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+			return -EPROBE_DEFER;
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	}
+	if (size != sizeof(struct modem_smem_type)) {
+		dev_err(dev, "Get modem_smem pointer failed\n");
 		return -ENOMEM;
 	}
